## Search method

**trigrams** (trigrams)

## Rules (rule engineer and attributes)

- R-0009 [rejected] "linge machine" is the usage "machine", in orders, invoices and catalogue names alike; a usage stated on one side only, or a different one, is never the same product. — by rule-engineer (a marker needs a plain product beside the variant: 5 of 5 products it marks have none (e.g. LINA CLEAN LIQUIDE LINGE MACHINE 10L))
- R-0008 [shadow] "frmg" means "fromage". — by rule-engineer
- R-0007 [rejected] "stick" is the form "stick", in orders, invoices and catalogue names alike; a form stated on one side only, or a different one, is never the same product. — by rule-engineer (a marker needs a plain product beside the variant: 2 of 2 products it marks have none (e.g. NESQUIK CHOCOLAT EN POUDRE STICK))
- R-0006 [rejected] "machine" is the usage "machine", in orders, invoices and catalogue names alike; a usage stated on one side only, or a different one, is never the same product. — by rule-engineer (a marker needs a plain product beside the variant: 8 of 9 products it marks have none (e.g. ASTUCE NETTOYANT MACHINE A LAVER))
- R-0005 [rejected] "sach" means "sachet". — by rule-engineer (resolves only 1 new line(s) and brings 0 closer; the gate needs 2 resolved or 6 closer)
- R-0004 [rejected] "frs" means "fraise". — by rule-engineer (resolves only 1 new line(s) and brings 0 closer; the gate needs 2 resolved or 6 closer)
- R-0003 [rejected] "fourre", "enrobe", "sandwich", "gaufrette", "moulu", "soluble" each name a form, in orders, invoices and catalogue names alike; two texts whose form differs are never the same product. — by muse-spark-profile (would make 1 pair(s) of different products read the same)
- R-0002 [live] "blanc", "white", "noir", "black" each name a colour, in orders, invoices and catalogue names alike; two texts whose colour differs are never the same product. — by muse-spark-profile
- R-0001 [rejected] "chocolat", "vanille", "fraise", "abricot", "caramel", "pistache", "ananas", "thon", "menthe", "citron" each name a flavour, in orders, invoices and catalogue names alike; two texts whose flavour differs are never the same product. — by muse-spark-profile (disagreed in shadow mode on « CHOC STORY SOLEO »)

